# FW5 names simblk.py can't find: the read sources FW5 adds (A5-A9 the
# game's MBC3 clock writes, BB $7FD3 + $7FD4, B5 eight command bits where
# FW4 has five, B8 two status bits, A0 the timer, which is a block of its
# own), the ICAP's output (simblk keys the block's pins differently), and
# what FW5 adds here: OUTPUT A5-A9 (the clock values the game's MBC3 latch
# copies), the OUTPUT A1 decode that starts the timer and the D0-D3 decode
# pb_periph's ICAP data write shares, and OUTPUT EF's decode (gb_bus's
# copy of the busy flag reads it)
